{
  "dom_id": "step-q176019",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "The solution to the inequality $-2x+10\\ge 4$ is $x${{field-1}}{{field-2}}.",
  "worked_solution": "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $10$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+10 & \\ge 4 \\\\ -2x+10-10 & \\ge 4-10 \\\\ -2x+0 & \\ge -6 \\\\ -2x & \\ge -6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $-2.$ \n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x\\,\\, & \\ge \\,\\,-6 \\\\ \\frac{-2x}{-2}\\, & \\le \\,\\,\\frac{-6}{-2} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-2}x}{\\cancel{-2}}\\, & \\le \\,\\,3 \\\\ x\\,\\, & \\le \\,3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\le 3.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
